      "@type": "schema:ScholarlyArticle",
      "url": "https://doi.org/10.1038/s41592-020-01008-z",
      "schema:name": "nnU-Net: a self-configuring method for deep learning-based biomedical image segmentation. Nature Methods, 2021."
    }
  ],
  "mach:governance": "academic",
  "mach:foundation": "Division of Medical Image Computing, DKFZ (Fabian Isensee et al.)",
  "mach:category": "ai-ml-models",
  "mach:subcategory": "imaging-model",
  "mach:maturity": "production",
  "mach:judgement": "Adopt",
  "mach:judgementReason": "The undisputed benchmark for medical image segmentation. nnU-Net's self-configuring approach — automatically tuning architecture, preprocessing, and post-processing per dataset — has dominated MICCAI segmentation challenges since 2018 and is cited in thousands of papers. Nature Methods 2021 publication, Apache-2.0, pip-installable (nnunetv2), 8,000+ GitHub stars. Any new medical segmentation project should benchmark against or build on nnU-Net before choosing an alternative. Academic governance is the only caveat; the principal author (Fabian Isensee) is exceptionally active.",
  "mach:editorialReviewedAt": "2026-05-11",
